; DERIVED, not verbatim. Written by this library (FX-1 pass 1, schema lane) from sections 9, 11.3
; and 11.4 of PICS 1.1 Label Distribution (W3C REC 1996-10-31). The source grammars are in
; http-request-s11-3.verbatim.txt and http-response-s11-4.verbatim.txt. Executed by
; check-grammar.derived.py TOGETHER WITH labels.derived.abnf (it uses labellist and alphanumpm
; and the lex- rules of that file). Same two layers as labels.derived.abnf; here "{" and "}" are
; delimiter tokens as well as "(" ")". Section 9 (RFC-822 Headers) gives no BNF beyond
; "PICS-Label: <labellist>"; label-header below is the section 11.4 production. The section 12.2
; productions of the same names (extension, token, token-or-quoted-string) are in
; bureau-query.derived.abnf under a bq- prefix (README.md, A9).

; request-header :: 'Protocol-Request: {PICS-1.1 {params ' [completeness] extension* services '}}'
request-header = "Protocol-Request:" "{" "PICS-1.1" "{" "params" [ completeness ] *extension services "}" "}"
completeness   = "minimal" / "short" / "full" / "signed"
; The same production with the prose of section 11.3 applied: "any alphanumeric string may be used
; for a value of the completeness option". A request that only this rule accepts is a place where
; the grammar and the prose disagree (A10).
request-header-prose = "Protocol-Request:" "{" "PICS-1.1" "{" "params" [ lex-token ] *extension services "}" "}"
; extension :: '{' token-or-quoted-string+ '}' where the first token-or-quoted-string is not 'services'.
; The exclusion is NOT expressible in ABNF; check-grammar.derived.py applies it as the named hook
; EXCLUDE on lex-first-token (the texts that rule may not match). A quoted first item "services"
; is a quoted string, not the token services, and is allowed.
extension      = "{" lex-first-token *token-or-quoted-string "}"
               / "{" lex-quotedname *token-or-quoted-string "}"
token-or-quoted-string = lex-token / lex-quotedname
lex-first-token = 1*alphanumpm
lex-token      = 1*alphanumpm
services       = "{" "services" 1*lex-quotedurl "}"

; protocol-header :: 'Protocol: {PICS-1.1 {headers PICS-Label}}'
protocol-header = "Protocol:" "{" "PICS-1.1" "{" "headers" "PICS-Label" "}" "}"
; label-header :: 'PICS-Label: ' labellist
label-header   = "PICS-Label:" labellist
